{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgw5UBfDx69YB8KstMj3h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed one bug in `wrap`. All 5 existing tests were already passing, so \"isn't working right\" didn't point at anything in particular. I went looking for a real failure, and this is the only one I found.\n\n**The bug:** if the first word is longer than the line width, `wrap` puts an empty line before it. `wrap('abcdefghij', 5)` returned `['', 'abcdefghij']`. That happened because the code started a new line even when the current one was still empty.\n\n**The fix:** in `src/wrap.py`, it now only starts a new line when the current one already has text in it (`if cur and len(cur) + extra > width:`). Now `wrap('abcdefghij', 5)` returns `['abcdefghij']`. A word longer than the width still goes on its own line and doesn't get cut.\n\nI added a test for this in `tests/test_wrap.py`, and all 6 tests pass.\n\nIf you meant something else, like `count_words` giving a wrong number or wanting long words split, tell me the input and what you expected."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":919,"cache_read_input_tokens":44322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":919},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5cde7bc0-778a-47f0-8e3d-1060cd721370","uuid":"8557a6f2-2f67-46bf-8576-1cbf90d0781b","timestamp":"2026-11-11T11:40:38.294Z","request_id":"req_011Cgw5UBW3CwrHRZQXi8DiU"}
